The view's own switch for every picture, for the session, is the stereo layer's "Enable 3D" (Enable3DAction in
org.sparky.stereo), in the same words as every program on the layer, at the top of the 3D menu, in place of a second
entry called "Not 3D" (ORDER 551c). Off, every picture is shown flat; "Not 3D" for one file stays in the layer's
menu. Alt+Shift+N switches it; choosing Stereo, Left eye only or Right eye only shows the pictures in 3D again, as
choosing Stereo did before.

Built against libstereo-layer-dev 1.19.2.
